{"t_ms": 7931453, "conversation_id": "conv_fixed_early_proxy_s2_008", "turn_id": 1, "actor": "system", "event_type": "retrieval_result", "payload": {"passages": ["Guest Complaint Resolution\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nGuest satisfaction is our highest priority. Any concerns regarding room facilities, cleanliness, dining, or hotel services should be reported to the Front Desk immediately. The hotel aims to acknowledge complaints promptly and resolve most issues within a reasonable timeframe. If required, matters may be escalated to the Duty Manager for further assistance and resolution.", "# corpus/ \u2014 Hotel Documents\n\n**Owner: Lakshya**\n\n## What this folder is\n\nThe hotel's documents live here: the knowledge the assistant answers from. About 60 short \ndocuments covering things like pool and gym hours, check-in and check-out rules, menus, and \npolicies.\n\n## How to fill it\n\nSee the full instructions in `retrieval/README.md` (Step 1). In short:\n- Write ~60 short documents, one topic per file, as `.txt` or `.md`.\n- Make them realistic and varied.\n- Deliberately plant a few contradictions (e.g. one doc says the pool closes at 10 PM, \n  another says 9 PM) and keep a note of which ones, for a later experiment.\n\nThe index-building script reads every file in this folder, so anything you put here becomes \npart of the searchable knowledge.\n", "Housekeeping Schedule\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nDaily housekeeping services are provided between 9:00 AM and 5:00 PM. Guests who prefer not to be disturbed may activate the \"Do Not Disturb\" indicator outside their room. Additional cleaning requests or replenishment of towels and toiletries can be made by contacting housekeeping through the in-room telephone."], "scores": [0.7721070647239685, 0.9151121377944946, 0.9886218309402466], "filenames": ["08_guest_complaints.txt", "README.md", "15_housekeeping.txt"], "timing_policy": "fixed_early_proxy", "timing_trigger": "fixed_early_proxy", "user_end_kno